      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/GeiserX/Telegram-Archive\n\n### Category\n\nPython\n\n### Project Title\n\nSelf-hosted Telegram backup with a web viewer\n\n### Project Description\n\nA self-hosted backup for Telegram accounts. It stores your chats' messages and media in SQLite or PostgreSQL on your own machine on a schedule, including edits and deleted messages, and a web viewer lets you browse and search the archive.\n\n### Highlights\n\nTelegram Desktop's export is a one-off file. This one keeps running. It saves each edit next to the earlier text and keeps deleted messages, marked as deleted. It can import a Desktop export, back up several accounts into one archive, and runs from pip or in read-only containers for amd64 and arm64.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GeiserX/Telegram-Archive/main/docker-compose.yml\n# put TELEGRAM_API_ID, TELEGRAM_API_HASH, TELEGRAM_PHONE, VIEWER_USERNAME and VIEWER_PASSWORD in .env\nmkdir -p data && sudo chown -R 1000:1000 data\ndocker compose run --rm telegram-backup python -m telegram_archive auth\ndocker compose up -d\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/GeiserX/Telegram-Archive/main/docs/images/screenshots/chat-desktop.png\n",
